# Production environment files.
#
# Every variant, not just the exact name. `.env.prod` alone did not cover
# `.env.prod.bak-022415`, a timestamped copy left beside it by an earlier edit - and
# `git add -A` duly staged it, database password and all. Caught before it was committed,
# but only by looking; a secret in git history is not removed by deleting the file later.
#
# `.env.prod.example` is re-included: it is the template and holds only placeholders.
.env.prod
.env.prod.*
!.env.prod.example
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Stored uploads: incident evidence, permit documents, equipment photos, generated
# report PDFs. Runtime data, and in production it is customer data - it belongs on a
# volume, never in the repository. A .gitkeep preserves the directory itself.
uploads/*
!uploads/.gitkeep

# deploy/deployment.sh records which release it replaced, for rollback.sh.
.releases/
